# Add-in runtime files must never be served stale: Outlook's WebView caches
# them aggressively, and a stale commands.js after an update breaks signature
# insertion silently (no error shown to the user). "no-cache" still permits
# conditional requests (ETag / Last-Modified -> 304), so clients revalidate
# cheaply on every load instead of reusing an outdated copy.
#
# X-Frame-Options inherited from public/.htaccess is dropped because a browser
# refuses these pages in a cross-origin iframe with it. They expose nothing
# without the key in their own URL.
<IfModule mod_headers.c>
    Header set Cache-Control "no-cache, must-revalidate"
    Header unset X-Frame-Options
</IfModule>
